			<div class="content" id="post-content-4862384">
									

<p>Thanks for the crit Red</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The store itself is now owned by a parent company (potentially MC&amp;D). The reason there is only 1 gun a week is to cause customers to keep coming back to the store and potentially spend more money than they originally anticipated. Basically, its just a greedy company. Its behind a glass case because they want people's eyes to be drawn to it an make it look valuable. The gun is made anomalous by unknown means which the foundation will try to investigate. Its only closed for a half hour because the greedy company wants to make a lot of money. As for the minor anomalies, its mostly quality of life stuff for the employee and the building, like a restocking fridge in the break room, and an indestructible firing gallery.</p>
<p>The foundation found the place after investigating a surge in anomalous weapons in the local area. The 1 employee thing is again meant to show the greedy company wanting to make as little spending as they can, but I can change the 1 employee if you feel it would be better. The person no longer thinks the guns are non-anomalous, but the dont talk about their job outside of work because they feel it would be very boring to do so because to them it feels like an accountant talking about how they filed their drawer and such, you understand? The foundation now actively tries to shut down the building through several means, but they keep getting reverted because of the company's seemingly endless supply of funds. They do eventually shut it down by just demolishing it and relocating the shooting gallery. As for the hook, IDK. I'm having trouble finding a new one. Any ideas?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks for the Crit</p>

